{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"weak-collections","title":"WeakMap, WeakSet & WeakRef","group":"Collections & Iteration","order":35,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Weak collections hold their keys <em>weakly</em>: if nothing else references a key object, it can be garbage-collected and its entry silently disappears.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th><code>Map</code> / <code>Set</code></th><th><code>WeakMap</code> / <code>WeakSet</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Keys</td><td>Anything</td><td>Objects (and non-registered symbols) only</td></tr><tr><td>Keeps key alive?</td><td>Yes — strong reference</td><td>No — weak reference</td></tr><tr><td>Iterable / <code>size</code>?</td><td>Yes</td><td>No (contents depend on the GC)</td></tr><tr><td>Methods</td><td>Full API</td><td><code>get/set/has/delete</code> · <code>add/has/delete</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-lock\"></i>Use case: private data / metadata per object</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const privateData = new WeakMap();\nclass Person {\n  constructor(name, ssn) {\n    this.name = name;\n    privateData.set(this, { ssn });   // disappears when the Person is collected\n  }\n  lastFour() { return privateData.get(this).ssn.slice(-4); }\n}\nconst p = new Person(\"Asha\", \"123-45-6789\");\nconsole.log(p.lastFour(), p);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>6789 Person { name: 'Asha' }</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-database\"></i>Use case: caching without leaks</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const cache = new WeakMap();\nfunction expensiveSummary(obj) {\n  if (cache.has(obj)) return cache.get(obj) + \" (cached)\";\n  const result = `keys=${Object.keys(obj).length}`;\n  cache.set(obj, result);\n  return result;\n}\nconst report = { a: 1, b: 2 };\nconsole.log(expensiveSummary(report));\nconsole.log(expensiveSummary(report));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>keys=2\nkeys=2 (cached)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-tag\"></i>WeakSet: tagging objects</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const visited = new WeakSet();\nfunction visit(node) {\n  if (visited.has(node)) return \"already visited\";\n  visited.add(node);\n  return \"visiting\";\n}\nconst node = {};\nconsole.log(visit(node), \"/\", visit(node));\ntry {\n  visited.add(\"string\");\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.message);\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>visiting / already visited\nInvalid value used in weak set</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-ghost-2\"></i>WeakRef and FinalizationRegistry (ES2021)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>let big = { data: \"large object\" };\nconst ref = new WeakRef(big);\nconsole.log(ref.deref()?.data);   // still alive\nbig = null;                       // now only weakly reachable — may be collected later\nconst registry = new FinalizationRegistry((label) =&gt; console.log(\"collected\", label));\nregistry.register({}, \"temp object\");</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>large object</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>GC timing is unpredictable: <code>deref()</code> may return the object long after you dropped it, and finalizers may never run. Use these only for caches and resource cleanup hints — never for program logic.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Why can't you iterate a WeakMap?</summary><div><p>Its entries vanish whenever the garbage collector reclaims a key, which happens at non-deterministic times. Exposing iteration or <code>size</code> would make program behaviour depend on GC timing, so the API deliberately hides them.</p></div></details></section>"}